cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ebm-pytorch in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ebm-pytorch: training and using energy-based models in PyTorch"
abstract: >-
  A narrow, reliable PyTorch library for energy-based models: contrastive
  divergence and persistent CD, score matching (denoising, sliced, NCSN),
  noise-contrastive estimation, diffusion recovery likelihood, and JEM;
  Langevin/MALA/HMC and Gibbs-with-Gradients samplers; energy composition;
  and an evaluation stack (AIS-bracketed log Z, FID, MMD, OOD AUROC,
  bits-per-dim).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: David
    email: david@cortify.io
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/davidkhjo/ebm-pytorch"
url: "https://davidkhjo.github.io/ebm-pytorch/"
keywords:
  - energy-based-models
  - ebm
  - generative-models
  - langevin-dynamics
  - contrastive-divergence
  - score-matching
  - pytorch
